# build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.o
*.ko
*.mod
*.mod.c
*.symvers
*.order
.tmp_versions/

# editor / working files
*.pre-*
*.orig-backup
*.bak
*~

# things that must never be committed: this project's provisioning file
# carries a wifi PSK and a password hash. Keep the example, never the real one.
custom.toml
*.key
id_*
authorized_keys

# Experimental Pi's OSD, recovered from the captured original card. The driver
# they left behind is GPL and lives in driver/; this is not — `osd` is their
# proprietary 32-bit binary, and multi_switch.sh ships with it. Kept locally
# because the binary is unstripped and is the best surviving documentation of
# the XPi protocol, but this repo is public, so it must not be pushed.
# Anchored: unanchored `osd.cfg` would also swallow a documentation excerpt
# committed under docs/ or config/, and this repo mines that file (piboy-fand's
# fan bands and piboy-vold's volume curve both came out of it).
/vendor-osd/

# private to one machine: disk images, their checksums, rom listings
*.pcl
*.pcl.zstd
MANIFEST.txt
capture.log
verify-diff.txt
duplicates-found.txt
partition-table.sfdisk
